      </section>
      <h2 id="installing-ocp-agent-iscsi-files_installing-using-iscsi" class="group scroll-mt-20">Creating the installation files<a href="#installing-ocp-agent-iscsi-files_installing-using-iscsi" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">Generate the ISO image and create an iPXE script to upload to your iSCSI target.</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Create the agent image by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ openshift-install --dir <install_directory> agent create image"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Create an iPXE script by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ cat << EOF > agent.ipxe\n!ipxe\nset initiator-iqn <iscsi_initiator_base>:\\${hostname}\nsanboot --keep iscsi:<iscsi_network_subnet>.1::::<iscsi_target_base>:\\${hostname}\nEOF"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;iscsi_initiator_base&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the iSCSI initiator name on the host that is booting the ISO. This name can also be used by the iSCSI target.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;iscsi_network_subnet&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the IP address of the iSCSI target.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;iscsi_target_base&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the iSCSI target name. This name can be the same as the initiator name.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      <CodeBlock code={"$ cat << EOF > agent.ipxe\n!ipxe\nset initiator-iqn iqn.2023-01.com.example:\\${hostname}\nsanboot --keep iscsi:192.168.45.1::::iqn.2023-01.com.example:\\${hostname}\nEOF"} lang="terminal" title="Example Command" />
      </li>
      </ol>
